# Foundry Ventures — environment reference
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. `.env*` is git-ignored; this example file
# is the only one committed, and it must never contain a real value.
#
# Every variable below is read somewhere in `src/` or `scripts/`; nothing here is
# aspirational. There are deliberately NO `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables: no secret,
# no recipient address and no CMS token may ever reach the client bundle (§23).
# Everything listed is server-only. The ones marked SECRET must come from a
# secret store (GitHub Actions secrets, the host's env UI) and never from a file
# in the repository.
#
# Which of these are *required* depends on the surface you are running:
#   - a local dev server needs none of them;
#   - the production content gate (`pnpm content:gate`) requires the ones marked
#     [gate];
#   - `/pitch`, `/api/draft/*`, `/api/revalidate` and `/api/pitch/maintenance`
#     each disable themselves when their own variables are absent.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Publishing policy
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Forces the publication policy instead of inferring it (src/content/context.ts).
#   production  renders only owner-approved fields — the public site
#   preview     renders unapproved/unpublished records behind a banner, noindex
# Unset, the resolution order is: draft-mode cookie → NODE_ENV. So `next dev`
# is preview and a production runtime is production. CI and the deploy gate set
# it explicitly so nothing depends on inference.
# [gate] must be exactly "production".
FOUNDRY_POLICY_MODE=preview

# Single-hop canonical host normalisation in src/middleware.ts: HTTP or the apex
# host 308-redirect to https://www.foundryventures.ai. Off by default so local
# development and preview deployments are not redirected off their own host.
# [gate] must be exactly "1".
FOUNDRY_ENFORCE_CANONICAL_HOST=0


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Synthetic end-to-end fixtures — TEST ONLY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# src/content/seed/fixtures.ts contains FICTIONAL companies, people and posts so
# Playwright can exercise filters, detail routes and related content against
# approved-looking records. Two independent switches are required to load it, and
# the production gate fails if either is set. Never set these outside a test run.
#
# FOUNDRY_CONTENT_FIXTURE=e2e
# FOUNDRY_ALLOW_FIXTURES=1


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Draft preview
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SECRET. Shared secret for GET /api/draft/enable?secret=…&redirect=/some/path.
# When unset the endpoint answers 404 to every method — a deployment without this
# value has no preview surface at all. /api/draft/disable never needs it.
# Use a long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# [gate] must be set.
DRAFT_MODE_SECRET=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sanity CMS (optional — the local seed adapter is the default)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The Sanity adapter activates only when BOTH SANITY_PROJECT_ID and
# SANITY_DATASET are set (src/content/adapters/sanity.ts). With either absent the
# site builds and tests entirely from src/content/seed/**, with no credentials.

SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
SANITY_DATASET=

# Optional. Defaults to 2024-10-01.
SANITY_API_VERSION=

# SECRET. Read token. Its presence switches the client to the `drafts`
# perspective and bypasses the CDN, so leave it unset for a public production
# read of published documents only.
SANITY_READ_TOKEN=

# SECRET. Verifies the `sanity-webhook-signature` header on POST /api/revalidate.
# When unset the webhook answers 404 to every method.
# [gate] must be set.
SANITY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# The Sanity Studio is a separate project and reads its own pair of variables.
# They are listed here only because src/sanity/schema-types.ts documents them;
# this application never reads them.
# SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=
# SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pitch pipeline (src/lib/pitch)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# checkPitchReadiness() in src/lib/pitch/config.ts turns these into a list of
# problems. In production, any problem means /pitch renders the contact fallback
# instead of a form — a founder must never write a pitch into a form that drops
# it. In development the same check usually fails and the form is still shown,
# because the file store and log notifier genuinely work end to end locally.

# SECRET (recipient addresses are not public). Comma- or semicolon-separated
# list of internal addresses that receive the "a pitch arrived" notification.
# Entries that do not look like an email address are dropped silently.
# [gate] required.
PITCH_RECIPIENTS=

# SECRET. Single address that receives dead-lettered notifications — the pitch
# that could not be delivered after retries. Without it those failures are
# silent, which is the failure mode the outbox exists to prevent.
# [gate] required.
PITCH_ESCALATION_EMAIL=

# SECRET. Verified sender address at the email provider. Required whenever
# RESEND_API_KEY is set.
# [gate] required.
PITCH_FROM_EMAIL=

# SECRET. Transactional email provider key. When unset the notifier falls back
# to the `log` driver, which only records that a notification would have been
# sent — correct for development, never acceptable in production.
# [gate] required.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# SECRET. Per-deployment salt for the irreversible submitter fingerprint used for
# rate limiting and duplicate detection. A per-environment value keeps the hash
# from being correlated across environments. Defaults to "foundry-dev-salt",
# which the readiness check treats as "not configured".
# [gate] required, and must not be the development default.
PITCH_FINGERPRINT_SALT=

# Storage driver: "file" (default) or "memory". `memory` is not durable and is
# rejected by the readiness check. `file` is also rejected when VERCEL=1, because
# a serverless filesystem does not survive the request.
PITCH_STORE_DRIVER=file

# Directory for the file driver, relative to the working directory.
# Defaults to .data/pitch (git-ignored, written 0600).
PITCH_STORE_DIR=.data/pitch

# Retention window in days before a stored submission is purged by
# POST /api/pitch/maintenance. Defaults to 730 and must stay in step with the
# figure stated in the privacy notice (src/content/seed/legal.ts).
PITCH_RETENTION_DAYS=730

# Optional. Base URL of the internal tool where a reviewer opens a submission.
# When set, the notification email includes a link built from it.
PITCH_REVIEW_URL_BASE=

# SECRET. Bearer secret for POST /api/pitch/maintenance (retention purge +
# outbox retry, safe to run on a cron). When unset the endpoint answers 404 to
# every method. Not part of the content gate, but a deployment without it never
# purges expired submissions or retries failed notifications.
PITCH_MAINTENANCE_SECRET=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set by the platform — do not set these yourself
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NODE_ENV  set by next/vitest/playwright. It is the fallback that decides the
#           policy mode when FOUNDRY_POLICY_MODE is absent.
# VERCEL    set to "1" by Vercel. The pitch readiness check uses it to reject the
#           ephemeral filesystem store on a serverless host.

# Indexing is opt-in (docs/decisions.md D-035). Leave unset everywhere except the
# real production deployment: unset means robots.txt disallows all, every route
# emits noindex metadata, and the proxy sends X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow.
# Set at BUILD time as well as runtime, so prerendered metadata and robots.txt agree.
# FOUNDRY_INDEXABLE=1
